{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3475","id":4520036893,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz888AAAABDWpKHQ","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3475","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3475.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3475.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3475","number":3475,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"db: report blocking node count when destroying a user","user":{"login":"YpNo","id":883643,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MzY0Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/883643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo","html_url":"https://github.com/YpNo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Deleting a user that still owns nodes fails with a bare \"user still has nodes\".\r\nThe `headscale users destroy` prompt only mentions pre-auth keys, so the error\r\nreads like something went wrong rather than a precondition. This wraps\r\n`ErrUserStillHasNodes` with the number of nodes that block the deletion:\r\n\r\n    deleting user: user still has nodes: 3 node(s) must be deleted or moved to another user first\r\n\r\n`errors.Is` still matches the sentinel, so the API keeps returning 400 and the\r\nexisting tests pass unchanged.\r\n\r\nWhile here, the `TestDestroyUserErrors` table now runs on Postgres as well as\r\nSQLite. User deletion relies on foreign-key actions (cascade on `nodes.user_id`,\r\nset-null on `pre_auth_keys.user_id`) that come from the hand-written SQLite\r\nschema on one side and GORM AutoMigrate on the other, and nothing exercised the\r\nPostgres side. The Postgres variant uses the existing `newPostgresTestDB`\r\nhelper and skips when no local server can be started, like the other Postgres\r\ntests.\r\n\r\n- [x] have read the CONTRIBUTING.md file\r\n- [ ] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\r\n- [x] added unit tests\r\n- [ ] added integration tests\r\n- [ ] updated documentation if needed\r\n- [x] updated CHANGELOG.md","created_at":"2026-09-13T17:50:09Z","updated_at":"2026-09-25T21:56:03Z","closed_at":"2026-09-25T21:56:02Z","merged_at":"2026-09-25T21:56:02Z","merge_commit_sha":"04d1e3c83fb0ca8e97079ed9652133c6f76303ba","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"juanfont","id":181059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTA1OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"ohdearaugustin","id":14001491,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDAxNDkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1400149